255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 168 0 R
/T (to help students, faculty members, and campus visitors explore selected areas of the IIIT Bhopal campus. Rather than relying on disconnected static floor plans or generic satellite maps, users can control a custom student avatar within a responsive 2.5D virtual environment. The application brings spatial navigation, comprehensive facility information, and institutional directory lookups into a unified, lightweight interface.)
/E (to help students, faculty members, and campus visitors explore selected areas of the IIIT Bhopal campus. Rather than relying on disconnected static floor plans or generic satellite maps, users can control a custom student avatar within a responsive 2.5D virtual environment. The application brings spatial navigation, comprehensive facility information, and institutional directory lookups into a unified, lightweight interface.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 168 0 R
/T (On the client side, the frontend integrates React 18 with the Phaser 3 game engine through an asynchronous decoupled event bus. React manages high-level routing, search overlays, heads-up displays, and detailed modal views, while Phaser handles world rendering, player movement, physics collisions, and camera tracking. Campus buildings are rasterized onto an internal coordinate grid where building boundaries act as solid colliders, preventing the avatar from passing through walls while allowing free exploration across pathways.)
/E (On the client side, the frontend integrates React 18 with the Phaser 3 game engine through an asynchronous decoupled event bus. React manages high-level routing, search overlays, heads-up displays, and detailed modal views, while Phaser handles world rendering, player movement, physics collisions, and camera tracking. Campus buildings are rasterized onto an internal coordinate grid where building boundaries act as solid colliders, preventing the avatar from passing through walls while allowing free exploration across pathways.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 168 0 R
/T (The backend is built with Node.js and Express, exposing structured REST endpoints for campus configuration, location records, spatial search, and route calculation. It includes a resilient dual-mode architecture that operates in a zero-dependency in-memory demo mode when a database connection is absent, while seamlessly integrating with MongoDB via Mongoose when configured. The system incorporates an A* pathfinding engine that computes collision-free walking trajectories, calculates realistic physical distances in meters, and estimates transit times at human walking speeds.)
/E (The backend is built with Node.js and Express, exposing structured REST endpoints for campus configuration, location records, spatial search, and route calculation. It includes a resilient dual-mode architecture that operates in a zero-dependency in-memory demo mode when a database connection is absent, while seamlessly integrating with MongoDB via Mongoose when configured. The system incorporates an A* pathfinding engine that computes collision-free walking trajectories, calculates realistic physical distances in meters, and estimates transit times at human walking speeds.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 168 0 R
/T (In addition to spatial exploration, the system includes an intelligent conversational assistant capable of executing map actions, along with real-time virtual classroom modules supporting WebSocket events and LiveKit WebRTC media streams. All 16 automated integration and unit test cases pass consistently in local verification runs. Keywords: virtual campus, metaverse, 2.5D environment, A* pathfinding, React, Phaser, Express, MongoDB, AI assistant, virtual classroom.)
/E (In addition to spatial exploration, the system includes an intelligent conversational assistant capable of executing map actions, along with real-time virtual classroom modules supporting WebSocket events and LiveKit WebRTC media streams. All 16 automated integration and unit test cases pass consistently in local verification runs. Keywords: virtual campus, metaverse, 2.5D environment, A* pathfinding, React, Phaser, Express, MongoDB, AI assistant, virtual classroom.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
