/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 171 0 R
/T (A modern university campus incorporates dozens of physically separated facilities, including academic lecture halls, departmental computing laboratories, libraries, administrative cells, and student hostels [22]. When new students or external visitors arrive at an institute, understanding the layout of these buildings and learning how to navigate between them is often challenging [22]. Conventional static layout maps provide an overview of the grounds, but they fail to support search, interactive route planning, or real-time spatial exploration in an accessible format [25].)
/E (A modern university campus incorporates dozens of physically separated facilities, including academic lecture halls, departmental computing laboratories, libraries, administrative cells, and student hostels [22]. When new students or external visitors arrive at an institute, understanding the layout of these buildings and learning how to navigate between them is often challenging [22]. Conventional static layout maps provide an overview of the grounds, but they fail to support search, interactive route planning, or real-time spatial exploration in an accessible format [25].)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 171 0 R
/T (The term metaverse is widely applied across academic research and computing literature to denote persistent or interactive digital environments where users engage with spatially organized information and digital avatars [1], [2]. In this project, the concept is applied to create an accessible, browser-rendered 2.5D representation of selected facilities at IIIT Bhopal [8]. Rather than demanding heavy proprietary virtual reality headsets or computationally demanding 3D gaming hardware, the platform focuses on delivering practical, responsive campus exploration on standard consumer computers [8], [23].)
/E (The term metaverse is widely applied across academic research and computing literature to denote persistent or interactive digital environments where users engage with spatially organized information and digital avatars [1], [2]. In this project, the concept is applied to create an accessible, browser-rendered 2.5D representation of selected facilities at IIIT Bhopal [8]. Rather than demanding heavy proprietary virtual reality headsets or computationally demanding 3D gaming hardware, the platform focuses on delivering practical, responsive campus exploration on standard consumer computers [8], [23].)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
