/T (The application architecture is organized into two primary workspaces: client and server [16]. The frontend client is developed with React 18, Vite, React Router, Tailwind CSS, and the Phaser 3 gaming framework [3], [4], [14], [15]. React governs top-level page views, navigation bars, search inputs, and modal interfaces, while Phaser manages the 2.5D canvas, sprite movements, collision boundaries, and camera tracking [3], [4]. This division of responsibility allows standard web interface elements to coexist with the game loop without degrading rendering performance [4], [13].)
/E (The application architecture is organized into two primary workspaces: client and server [16]. The frontend client is developed with React 18, Vite, React Router, Tailwind CSS, and the Phaser 3 gaming framework [3], [4], [14], [15]. React governs top-level page views, navigation bars, search inputs, and modal interfaces, while Phaser manages the 2.5D canvas, sprite movements, collision boundaries, and camera tracking [3], [4]. This division of responsibility allows standard web interface elements to coexist with the game loop without degrading rendering performance [4], [13].)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 171 0 R
/T (The backend is engineered with Node.js and the Express framework to serve RESTful endpoints consumed by the client interface [16], [17]. Incoming network requests are routed to specialized controllers and services that manage location records, A* route calculations, assistant queries, user favourites, and virtual classroom sessions [17], [18]. By separating routing from underlying business logic, the server maintains clean modular boundaries that simplify long-term software maintenance and testing [18], [22].)
/E (The backend is engineered with Node.js and the Express framework to serve RESTful endpoints consumed by the client interface [16], [17]. Incoming network requests are routed to specialized controllers and services that manage location records, A* route calculations, assistant queries, user favourites, and virtual classroom sessions [17], [18]. By separating routing from underlying business logic, the server maintains clean modular boundaries that simplify long-term software maintenance and testing [18], [22].)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
