/E (across separate PDF circulars, static website directories, and generic web maps [7], [25]. When incoming students seek a specific lab or faculty room, they are forced to piece together information from disjointed sources [25]. Developing a unified browser-based virtual campus provides an intuitive bridge between visual layouts and facility details, allowing students to inspect rooms and plan walking routes within a single window [7], [25].)
