/T (Spatial wayfinding on digital grids is modeled as a formal graph search problem [10], [11], [24]. Dijkstra's algorithm guarantees the discovery of the shortest path on graphs with non- negative edge costs, but it expands uniformly outward in all directions, evaluating unpromising nodes [10], [24]. The A* algorithm refines Dijkstra's search by incorporating a heuristic estimation function that guides exploration toward the destination [11], [24].)
