/T (The standard evaluation function in A* is formulated as f\(n\) = g\(n\) + h\(n\), where g\(n\) represents the exact cumulative cost from the start node to candidate node n, and h\(n\) represents the heuristic estimate of remaining cost from node n to the goal [11], [12]. On a four-directional grid with uniform step costs, the Manhattan distance metric is mathematically admissible because it never overestimates the actual minimum grid distance required to reach the destination [11], [12].)
