/T (Navigating university campus facilities is often difficult for newly admitted students, visiting parents, and recruiting teams, particularly in institutions operating across transit premises. IIIT Bhopal operates from its transit campus at the MANIT Bhopal complex. Because academic blocks, departmental laboratories, and administrative offices are located across different sections, newcomers frequently struggle to locate lecture rooms or understand available amenities. Traditional paper maps and static PDF documents provide no active route calculation, no intelligent search, and no dynamic facility guidance. This project addresses this problem by developing an interactive, browser-accessible 2.5D virtual campus application that combines spatial visualization, automated pathfinding, directory lookups, and virtual classroom collaboration into a unified interface.)
/E (Navigating university campus facilities is often difficult for newly admitted students, visiting parents, and recruiting teams, particularly in institutions operating across transit premises. IIIT Bhopal operates from its transit campus at the MANIT Bhopal complex. Because academic blocks, departmental laboratories, and administrative offices are located across different sections, newcomers frequently struggle to locate lecture rooms or understand available amenities. Traditional paper maps and static PDF documents provide no active route calculation, no intelligent search, and no dynamic facility guidance. This project addresses this problem by developing an interactive, browser-accessible 2.5D virtual campus application that combines spatial visualization, automated pathfinding, directory lookups, and virtual classroom collaboration into a unified interface.)
