<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 180 0 R
/T (To compute routes, world coordinates are converted to grid cells. If a start or target cell coincides with a solid building, the algorithm searches adjacent cells radially for the nearest walkable tile. A* evaluates candidate nodes using Manhattan distance heuristics. Once the goal is reached, the raw cell path is reconstructed via predecessor links and simplified using collinear cross products to eliminate redundant points along straight segments.)
/E (To compute routes, world coordinates are converted to grid cells. If a start or target cell coincides with a solid building, the algorithm searches adjacent cells radially for the nearest walkable tile. A* evaluates candidate nodes using Manhattan distance heuristics. Once the goal is reached, the raw cell path is reconstructed via predecessor links and simplified using collinear cross products to eliminate redundant points along straight segments.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5]
>>
