/Title (On the client side, the frontend integrates React 18 with the Phaser 3 game engine through an asynchronous decoupled event bus. React manages high-level routing, search overlays, heads-up displays, and detailed modal views, while Phaser handles world rendering, player movement, physics collisions, and camera tracking. Campus buildings are rasterized onto an internal coordinate grid where building boundaries act as solid colliders, preventing the avatar from passing through walls while allowing free exploration across pathways.)
