/Title (2 presents a literature review of relevant technologies and previous approaches [22]. Chapter 3 outlines the formal problem definition, project objectives, and requirement specifications [23]. Chapter 4 details the proposed methodology, system architecture, and module responsibilities [22]. Chapter 5 describes the core mathematical and algorithmic methods, including A* pathfinding and vector collinearity pruning [24]. Chapter 6 presents visual flowcharts, block diagrams, and data flow diagrams [23]. Chapter 7 details the software stack, implementation files, and database configuration [16], [17]. Chapter 8 evaluates the implementation results, automated test coverage, and known engineering limitations [23]. Chapter 9 concludes the study and identifies future research extensions [22].)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2660 0 R
/Prev 2676 0 R
>>
endobj
