/Title (Representing continuous physical ground as a discrete tile grid introduces an engineering trade-off between spatial fidelity and computational overhead [16], [24]. A coarse grid minimizes search space and memory consumption but can produce jagged paths or fail to register narrow walkways [24]. Conversely, a fine grid models intricate geometry accurately but exponentially expands the node count, requiring careful memory bounding during browser execution [16], [24].)
