/Title (Institutional websites and static digital floor plans remain standard tools for publishing official academic schedules and campus directories [8], [25]. However, traditional websites decouple descriptive text from spatial context, requiring users to mentally translate building codes into physical ground locations [25]. An interactive spatial atlas resolves this disconnect by anchoring descriptive facility metadata directly to clickable coordinates in a visual campus map [8], [25].)
